PATCH 234: faithful reconstruction of the MGAVIDEO HUD-text glyph plotter FUN_0000_1b98 -- the 1bpp
bit-expander font blitter (asm-verified vs re_out/fist_mga_image.bin 0x1b98-0x1d22).

Reached via 1b5c (patch 233) on the 6686 viewport status-text path (55ae -> [DGROUP:0x688] -> 1b5c -> 1b98).
It is the 1-bit-per-pixel twin of the byte-font blitter 1d5f (patch 131): same text-state struct at the
DGROUP:0x736 NEAR OFFSET, same control-char cursor ops, but the glyph pixels come from a 1bpp bitmap
expanded MSB-first (add ah,ah; sbb al,al; and al,cl; xor al,ch; stos) rather than a byte-per-pixel font.

Ghidra broke it two ways: (a) the DGROUP:0x736 host-pointer/width base-loss (the DAT_1000_c738 retrace
counter overlaps byte[2] of the 4-byte "pointer" -- see patch 233); (b) the blit inner loop was
mis-decompiled into an int-scaled CONCAT11 cascade against _DAT_2000_c226.  Rebuilt faithfully in the
DGROUP-offset model (SW(o) = word at g_mem+0x1c000 + (uint16)(s+o)); full asm map in the function comment.
The control-char switch (chars 7/8/a/d/c/e/f) is the same cursor arithmetic as 1d5f, case for case.

Advances the cascade past 1b98; the HUD status string now blits without the wild deref.  Cascade-only
(FIST_CASCADE default OFF) => BEHAVIOUR-NEUTRAL for the 19 verify flows (menu/dialog text draws via 1d5f).
Sources pristine; fist_mga.c via build/.  Portable C.
